menu "Prepared Workqueue Defaults"

config WORKQUEUE_WORKERS_PER_POOL
    usize "Maximum worker tasks per CPU"
    range 1 16
    default 4
    help
      Maximum normal worker tasks managed on each boot CPU. The manager
      creates workers in task context; prepared IRQ submissions never do.
      Keep the existing symbol so saved configurations retain their limit.

config KWORKNG_NORMAL_MAX_ACTIVE
    usize "Default threaded queue release limit per CPU"
    range 1 65535
    default 256
    help
      Ready-plus-running allowance per CPU, not the worker task count or
      the number of waiting submissions. Does not activate NG services.

config KWORKNG_BH_MAX_ACTIVE
    usize "Default BH queue release limit per CPU"
    range 1 65535
    default 64
    help
      Ready-plus-running allowance per CPU and BH priority queue.
      Does not activate NG services or replace existing workqueues.

config KFEAT_WORKQUEUE_BENCH
    bool "Run prepared workqueue benchmarks and soak instead of userspace"
    default n
    help
      Run the kernel release benchmark and mixed reuse workload after boot.
      Prints results independently of log level. Powers off after completion.
      This is a test-only entry, not a workqueue implementation selector.

config WORKQUEUE_SOAK_SECONDS
    usize "Prepared workqueue soak duration in seconds"
    depends on KFEAT_WORKQUEUE_BENCH
    range 0 86400
    default 1800
    help
      Zero runs only the benchmark rounds. Use an external timeout to detect
      hangs; the duration does not bound boot, measurement or final drain.

endmenu
